  "security_implications": "IV multiplexer directly selects among secret-related sources (external IV, cipher state, previous input data) and drives the IV register (iv_d). An unsafe iv_sel value can route secret plaintext or intermediate state into the IV path, or inadvertently apply clearing data, potentially enabling information leakage or denial of service. The default fallback to clearing data mitigates undriven states, but the generator of iv_sel must be free from faults to prevent unwanted exposure.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "aes_core.sv:341-351"
  ],
